course: dictionary
lesson: 5843
title: Words that sound alike
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A malapropism is a funny mistake. Someone uses a word that sounds like the right word but means something quite different. «He's the pineapple of politeness» should be «pinnacle», which means the highest point of something.
explain: The name comes from Mrs Malaprop, a character in Sheridan's play «The Rivals» (1775), who kept getting her words muddled. Readers laugh because the wrong word makes the sentence silly. If the words around a word do not make sense, a word may have been mixed up.
explain: Alice mixes up «antipodes» (the people on the opposite side of the Earth) with «antipathies» (strong dislikes). The two words sound alike but mean very different things, so her mix-up is a malapropism.
fact: A malapropism is a funny mistake that uses a word that sounds like the right word.
fact: The word comes from Mrs Malaprop, a character in Sheridan's play «The Rivals» (1775).
fact: «Pinnacle» means the highest point of something, but «pineapple» is a fruit.
fact: «Antipodes» means the people on the opposite side of the Earth; «antipathies» means strong dislikes.
fact: Malapropisms are often used to make people laugh in stories, comedy and real life.
exercise: What is a malapropism? | A word that means exactly the same as another word | *A funny mistake using a word that sounds like the right word | A long word found only in old dictionaries
exercise: In «He's the pineapple of politeness», which word was meant? | politics | *pinnacle | pineapple | polite
exercise: Mrs Malaprop is a character in which play? | Macbeth | Alice in Wonderland | The Mock Turtle's Lessons | *The Rivals
test: Alice mixes up «antipodes» with which word? | antidote | anthem | *antipathies | antibiotics
test: Why do readers laugh at a malapropism? | Because it is always written in capital letters | Because it is always in a poem | *Because the wrong word makes the sentence silly | Because the word is very long
exam: What does «antipodes» mean? | A sweet, juicy fruit | Strong dislikes | *The people on the opposite side of the Earth | The highest point of something
